Falsifies `system_tests::user::syscall_fuzzer_tests::seeded_syscalls_agree_with_the_shadow_model`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64 (the hunk is portable scheduler code).

The defect is the one `revocation_in_flight_tests` records, applied unchanged: the revocation sweep
for `PageFrame` stops reading `Thread::outgoing_cap`, so a frame staged in a parked `SEND_CAP`
survives `PageFrame::REVOKE` and the next `RECEIVE_CAP` files it in the receiver's table. It is one
of the six defects milestone 752 (a seeded syscall driver with a shadow model) was measured
against; the other five are in that block's table, with the seed and call each turned red.

Expected to fail: seed 342 (corpus), step 64, `RECEIVE_CAP` returns `x1 = 6` (the revoked frame's
new slot) where the shadow model says `NO_CAP`, reported as `syscall fuzzer: seed 0x156 step 64:
actor 3 Invoke { slot: 1, method: 3, ... } answered ...`. Replayed red on aarch64 on 2026-10-04 (UTC)
by the lane for milestone 752 at seed 5, step 39. After §246 (a plain `RECEIVE` never takes a
capability), a PROVISIONAL number, the walk diverged and seed 5 stayed green, so PR #1611 swept 2,000
seeds under this patch, found seed 342, added it to the corpus, and replayed it red on aarch64.

Regenerated 2026-10-04 (UTC) by the lane for the proposal "capability lookup off the global lock",
which moved each thread's capability table out of `Thread` and behind its own lock: the sweep now
iterates `(thread, table)` pairs, so the old hunk no longer matched. Same removal, same defect; the
added `let _ = t;` only keeps the patched build free of an unused-variable warning.
Replayed red on aarch64 the same day: seed 5, step 39, `regs: [5, ...]` against the model's `NO_CAP`.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched.rs b/kernel/src/sched.rs
--- a/kernel/src/sched.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched.rs
@@ -4374,9 +4374,7 @@ fn delete_page_frame_caps_where(matches: impl Fn(&crate::cap::Object) -> bool) {
     };
     for (t, caps) in sched.threads.iter_mut_with_capabilities() {
         caps.lock().delete_matching(&matches);
-        if matches!(t.outgoing_cap, Some(c) if matches(&c.object)) {
-            t.outgoing_cap = None;
-        }
+        let _ = t;
     }
 }
 
